            <ArticleTitle>Sickle cell crisis and endothelin antagonists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>225-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sickle cell crisis may be more complex than a vaso-occlusive event in response to hypoxia. Endothelin-1 (ET-1) is a potent vasoconstrictor and mitogen secreted in response to hypoxia. ET-1 contributes to the vaso-occlusion and inflammation in sickle cell crisis. ET-1 antagonists may be useful in the prevention and treatment of crisis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
